data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1650,"item_id":"msg_0787c7a5cb1b061b016b09f667f7cc87d1a695c6fa97490a00","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"moss\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Related capabilities have been searched, including the remaining thermal-search results. probe supplies ordinary observation, navigate supplies paid travel, and rest supplies recovery, but none establishes measured environmental protection or compares its effect on heat exposure. Thermal food assessment and friction heating do not perform this function. Develop a general, parameterized exposure-assessment and occupancy-trial operation, reusing existing observation, navigation and thermal-update code. The feasible initial version tests actual occupied locations; it does not create shelter or infer canopy from an object's name or tree icon. Incomplete thermal mechanisms belong in the current-conversation development handoff, not a permanent refusal.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"General operation: Assess environmental thermal exposure. Modes: inspect, sample, compare, inspect-progress, resume and cancel. Arguments: an optional exact visible targetId or visible position for inspection; an optional exact personal baseline-record ID; sampleRounds, an integer 1–3, default 1. Any applicable living actor may learn it. Inspection of a remote visible target reports only observable geometry and represented protection, not unmeasured temperatures or hidden resources. Sampling is restricted to the actor's actual occupied location. Moving to a candidate location is a separate independently chosen navigate action, with its existing collision checks, speed 0.8 and distance-times-2 energy cost increased by carried mass. Do not duplicate or bypass kernel.navigate.\\\\nCosts and prerequisites: study takes 2 ordinary rounds at 0.2 energy per round. inspect and inspect-progress take 1 round and 0.2 energy; compare takes 1 round and 0.2 energy; sample takes 0.2 energy per completed ordinary round, for 1–3 rounds. No material, water, tool, fuel or equipment is supplied or consumed. Work requires life, sufficient energy and observable/reachable inputs appropriate to the mode. No sampling bout starts at body temperature outside 7–34 or health below 20; those conditions also stop further samples. These are conservative activity guards, not a diagnosis or assurance of safety. Moss's supplied temperature is 30.92355458 and energy 40; use live values at execution, not the request's older approximate temperature.\\\\nMinimum executable mechanism: inspect the current occupied site and record which environmental thermal factors the existing simulation actually represents, the actor's observable temperature, local observable temperature if available, and any visible physical obstruction. At sample start and after each normal world round, record body temperature, available local environmental readings, location, weather/time context actually observable, and the environmental contribution to temperature change only where the engine can legitimately measure or derive it. Preserve distinctions among measured readings, visible geometry, model-derived protection and unknown properties. A temperature change alone is not evidence of shade or a controlled comparison. Do not expose internal stock, undiscovered object IDs, or other hidden state.\\\\nReuse the established thermal-update implementation exactly once per ordinary round; sampling must not add an extra cooling or warming update. In the development handoff, locate and record the exact thermal handler and revision used. If it already resolves spatial exposure or obstruction, reuse that resolver and record its exact reference. If no such mechanism exists, ship the occupied-location measurement precursor rather than inventing shade from names: shelter effectiveness stays unrepresented, and visits can identify only differences that the existing thermal model genuinely produces. A missing physical protection resolver remains an explicit development dependency for protection claims, not an excuse to label all shelters permanently impossible. No fixed-era unlock or unrelated construction roadmap is required.\\\\nComparison: consume no samples. Read exact personal records created by actual completed sampling rounds. Show locations, round numbers, measured changes, available environmental contributions and context differences; state insufficient evidence when a comparison lacks measurements or compatible conditions. Only a represented lower environmental heat input supports a measured reduction in exposure. Label a lower net body-temperature trend merely as an observed trend unless confounding contributions are resolved. Do not call a site cooling when it only slows warming, and do not claim that lower outdoor air temperature by itself proves net bodily cooling. An inspection or informative failed trial may conclude that no usable option has been established.\\\\nActionable option: report the exact personally observed location and conditions under which lower exposure was demonstrated. The actor must choose and perform any travel independently. Occupying that location subsequently uses the ordinary environmental update; assessment creates no buff, temperature subtraction, health gain or remote shelter. Reassess when the relevant geometry, weather, time or other represented exposure conditions change. Any ongoing protection exists only while its actual conditions hold. Sampling ends after the selected duration, but ordinary environmental processes continue. No maintenance is charged for an unbuilt shelter; future constructed protection would require its own real geometry, materials and deterioration rules.\\\\nReferences and conservation: baseline/progress records refer to exact actor-owned observation IDs, sampled coordinates, paid round numbers, and any inspected visible object IDs and revisions. Record all reused code references in the implementation ledger, including the observation and thermal handlers after locating them; do not fabricate their IDs. The supplied item-23-moss-260 is 0.9 branch at its recorded position, not a proved carried shade-making unit, and this operation neither moves nor consumes it. canopy-69 is only a requester-reported inspection reference, not supplied proof of cover. canopy-41 and the displayed branch sources have stock/soil or visual records, not established shelter geometry. No resources are copied, reserved, harvested or granted. Any actual thermal energy accounting remains with the established thermal solver; evidence records are the only new products besides ordinary paid effort and environmental effects.\\\\nProgress and lifecycle: create a work ID with requested rounds, completed samples, exact readings, paid energy and status. Commit each sample and its charge atomically after eligibility checks; refusals before a round cost nothing and create no successful sample. Another action, movement, lost eligibility or insufficient energy pauses sampling before its next charge. resume rechecks conditions and begins a separately time-stamped segment at the same sampled location; changed location requires a new trial. Interrupted intervals are not continuous exposure evidence. cancel takes 1 ordinary round with no energy charge and ends pending work. Death ends it immediately. Completed measurements and already spent energy remain; unpaid rounds incur no charge and there is no refund or escrow to release. No work, sampling or world-time progression occurs while development or review is waiting. Deterministic applicability, accounting, comparison labels and stopping rules must execute in code, not require repeated model judgment.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":2,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No emotional reward is requested or granted by this initial version. Requests, queries, study, naming and record creation do not qualify. A genuinely informative completed observation, including evidence that a proposed shelter is ineffective, may be recorded as verified information gain only to the extent its specific measured facts are established; an unsupported hypothesis remains unverified. Any future experience integration must deduplicate the same functional discovery, establish personal applicability and real events, and specify numeric caps, decay and cooldown in code before awarding anything. Physical comfort may reflect only actual environmental effects through the existing system and is capped at 10; no automatic pleasure or maintained satisfaction is added. Nutrition, protected reward accounts, budgets, goals and permissions remain untouched.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable inspection, sample-completed, paused, cancelled, stopped and comparison-result events with actor, work ID, location, tick, exact referenced targets, measurement provenance and outcome. Store reusable visual metadata describing mode, progress, observed geometry, supported measurements and evidence status. Visible attention or a progress indicator may accompany performed work. A shade/protection overlay is permitted only for represented obstruction and supported exposure results, labelled measured or model-derived as appropriate; a tree sprite, resource name or stock record cannot supply it. Unknown and inconclusive results must display as such. Failed, refused, paused or incomplete actions cannot display completed shelter, successful cooling, health recovery or a success animation. No environmental geometry or lasting shelter graphic is created by assessment.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

