granted by this initial version. Requests, queries, study, naming and record creation do not qualify. A genuinely informative completed observation, including evidence that a proposed shelter is ineffective, may be recorded as verified information gain only to the extent its specific measured facts are established; an unsupported hypothesis remains unverified. Any future experience integration must deduplicate the same functional discovery, establish personal applicability and real events, and specify numeric caps, decay and cooldown in code before awarding anything. Physical comfort may reflect only actual environmental effects through the existing system and is capped at 10; no automatic pleasure or maintained satisfaction is added. Nutrition, protected reward accounts, budgets, goals and permissions remain untouched.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable inspection, sample-completed, paused, cancelled, stopped and comparison-result events with actor, work ID, location, tick, exact referenced targets, measurement provenance and outcome. Store reusable visual metadata describing mode, progress, observed geometry, supported measurements and evidence status. Visible attention or a progress indicator may accompany performed work. A shade/protection overlay is permitted only for represented obstruction and supported exposure results, labelled measured or model-derived as appropriate; a tree sprite, resource name or stock record cannot supply it. Unknown and inconclusive results must display as such. Failed, refused, paused or incomplete actions cannot display completed shelter, successful cooling, health recovery or a success animation. No environmental geometry or lasting shelter graphic is created by assessment.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}}

